In-app rules

\- Bug report chip/tab is the only way to send
structured doing / happened / expected fields plus SETTINGS\_FOR\_SUPPORT and
extended diagnostics.

\- Feedback (comments) may offer optional “Attach extra
troubleshooting details” (default OFF) when the product has a diagnostics
block; Feature request MUST NOT.

\- Feature request MUST NOT show extended diagnostics
checkbox — narrative and contact only (no audit trail by default).

\- Copy on the Feedback page states that bug reports
belong here so version, active page, and troubleshooting details can be
included. How-to questions use Help, not Feedback.



Web and Help KB rules

\- Support page Contact block MUST say bug reports use
Help → Feedback (or Settings → Feedback) in the app — not web mailto alone.

\- Web mailto\:feedback@ MAY remain for Feedback and
feature ideas with subject hint — MUST NOT describe web email as including
automatic diagnostics.

\- Help KB articles about bugs MUST point to in-app
Feedback; MUST NOT promote a generic contact form or contact@ as the primary
bug path.

\- If the product has no installed app (marketing-only
page), web copy states bugs cannot be triaged without the app — offer
Feedback/feature mailto only.

\- Website Support & feedback form report types are
Feedback and Feature request only — no Help/Support how-to type.



Anti-patterns (reject)

\- Web “Report a bug” page or form that mimics in-app
structured bug flow without diagnostics.

\- Help KB copy that says “email contact@ with your
version” instead of in-app Feedback.

\- Feature request flow that attaches extended audit
diagnostics by default.

\- Presenting web mailto and in-app Feedback as
interchangeable for bugs.

